{"type":"text","timestamp":1791836699319,"sessionID":"ses_ece35f86fffesd4mJKAFFHYPMt","part":{"id":"prt_131ca1b23001ehmX32ToBbze2C","sessionID":"ses_ece35f86fffesd4mJKAFFHYPMt","messageID":"msg_131ca175800122mVU1x6lM1inY","type":"text","text":"Now I have everything I need. Let me analyze the source request and produce the full Requirements Elicitation Package.\n\n**Source request:**\n> \"Where offline export is included in the product, the export service shall provide the selected report as a downloadable CSV file.\"\n\nLet me work through this carefully before writing.\n\n**Analysis:**\n- The source uses the EARS Optional Feature pattern (`Where ... the ... shall ...`) — correctly formed syntactically.\n- Key terms needing examination: \"offline export,\" \"selected report,\" \"downloadable CSV file,\" \"export service.\"\n- \"Selected report\" is ambiguous — selected by whom, from what, at what moment?\n- \"Downloadable\" is an interaction design term: does this mean the service exposes a download endpoint, the browser triggers a download, or the file is placed somewhere accessible?\n- The format \"CSV\" is specific, but no structural constraints on the CSV (encoding, delimiter, headers, quoting, line endings) are stated.\n- \"Offline export\" as a feature name needs confirmation — it likely means the export can occur without a live network connection to a server, but that's an assumption.\n- No failure/error behavior is stated for when the report cannot be exported.\n- The primary candidate can be marked `needs clarification` on several points, with a provisional sentence shown.","time":{"start":1791836691235,"end":1791836699319}}}
